   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Something that should already be done",
     "texto": [
      "The **perfect subjunctive** is **haya** + participle. It says that something already happened before now:\n\n- Ha llegado. → Espero que **haya llegado**.\n- Has aprobado. → Me alegro de que **hayas aprobado**.\n- No ha llamado. → Me extraña que no **haya llamado**.\n\nCompare: espero que **llegues** bien (the journey has not finished yet) and espero que **hayas llegado** bien (it should be over by now)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Forms of haber: haya, hayas, haya…",
     "texto": [
      "The six forms of **haber** in the subjunctive are: **haya, hayas, haya, hayamos, hayáis, hayan**. A **participle** follows: haya llegado, hayas comido, hayan salido.\n\nIrregular participles: hecho, dicho, escrito, visto, puesto, vuelto, abierto, roto.\n\nYou use it where the subjunctive is needed and the action is already done:\n\n- Reactions: Me alegro de que **hayas venido**.\n- Doubts: No creo que **haya salido**.\n- Finished future time: Llámame cuando **hayas terminado**.\n\nAfter **gracias por** the compound infinitive is used: gracias por **haber venido**."
     ],
